ccess and actual piece structure at execution. forest-vine-1 and canopy-18 are provenance references, not additional material inputs. manual-78-lin-459 is prior assessment evidence only. Do not assume surface-21-lin-113 is available: its retained compatibility finding is dated, its record is incomplete, and other work exists nearby. Require an explicitly selected, currently clear radius-0.2 work footprint within 0.65 reach, with all manipulated extents accessible and no intrusion on people, plants or reserved work. Movement to the site is separate paid activity.\\\\nSmallest executable release: a paid non-destructive assessment that resolves only physically observable piece boundaries, endpoints, continuity, accessible dimensions, uncertainty and candidate segment endpoints against exact source revisions. Discrete identifiers must denote observed physical pieces, not arbitrary divisions of stack quantity. Geometric measurement requires an implemented spatial measurement mechanism with declared units, resolution and uncertainty; a physical measuring aid, if required, must be explicitly referenced, available and used. Never derive length from inventory quantity, render scale, flexibility or a label. If the underlying material lacks physical geometry, implement that missing physical representation/observation mechanism in this handoff where reasonable; otherwise produce dated specific unresolved findings, not fabricated dimensions. This release must add actual piece/segment examination or measured geometry beyond the prior unresolved-prerequisite assessment, not merely rename it.\\\\nQuote before execution: personal study takes 2 world rounds at 0.2 energy per completed round. Assess costs 1 active round and 0.5 energy; inspect costs 1 active round and 0.2 energy. Non-destructive assessment/inspection consumes no material. Once supported geometry and a reversible wrapping mechanism exist, quote a bounded single wrap operation of 2 active rounds at 0.5 energy each: first position the explicitly selected portions, then perform one loose, unknotted wrap of the selected continuous vine segment around the selected branch portions. No cutting, splicing, adhesive, tool, anchor or additional stock is supplied. Decline to start wrapping when selected extents cannot support this exact operation; report the measured reason. The first release need not expose unsupported wrap or force operations, but their reasonable missing mechanics remain in this same development handoff rather than being rejected or replaced with a fixed unlock roadmap.\\\\nA wrap requires explicit source piece IDs, segment endpoints, current measurement record, world placement and live clearance. Reserve only the nominated real portions, with a ledger mapping all remaining material to original sources. Representation changes do not create material: allocated material remains conserved in the placed arrangement and cannot simultaneously be available in inventory. If amount-to-segment accounting cannot be supported, do not allocate arbitrary fractional lengths or begin wrapping. Use ground-supported accessible pieces only; no structural joint, load capacity, binding strength, permanent attachment or practical utility is inferred. Record actual placement and deformation, including an unsuccessful attempt.\\\\nSeparation is a separate opt-in operation, never automatic after wrapping. It requires a completed extant arrangement, explicit opposed branch selections, force direction, duration, force ceiling, displacement stop and a real supported method of measuring applied force with resolution/uncertainty. A normalized probe intensity is not a calibrated force. Any instrument, actuator or external support must have an exact available reference and explicit cost; none is granted. The executable contract must publish numerical low-force and displacement ceilings supported by the mechanism before enabling this operation. If calibration, safe force control or reaction support is absent, report those precise prerequisites and leave separation unavailable without a fictitious result. When supported, one bounded separation attempt costs 1 active round and 0.5 actor energy, plus explicitly quoted real device energy/wear if applicable. Record actual force trace, duration, displacement and observed slip, opening, damage or lack of detectable change; stop at the first ceiling. No extrapolation to breaking strength or future safety.\\\\nRecover is a separately selected, physically feasible unwrapping and local retrieval attempt, quoted at 1 active round and 0.5 energy for this single loose wrap. Inspection must expose any obstruction requiring a different operation before charging recovery. Transfer only actually recovered surviving portions to the appropriate reachable inventory or local ground state; preserve damage and residual placement. Nothing restores original geometry, strength or quantity automatically. Alteration, tearing or loss must be supported by actual mechanics and conserved into surviving pieces or source-linked debris, never silently deleted or regenerated.\\\\nExecution code must track processId, operation, exact source revisions, allocations, paid rounds/energy, completed manipulations, remaining work, geometry evidence and arrangementId. Validate prerequisites and sufficient energy before each atomic step; invalid calls cost nothing, while a performed examination with an inconclusive result pays its stated cost. Pauses for access changes, exhaustion or explicit interruption retain completed work and exact physical state without further charges. Resume uses the exact processId, revalidates conditions and pays only remaining steps. Cancel before a paid step has no cost; later cancellation releases unused locks and leaves placed material and paid work intact. Cancellation is not free recovery. Death stops active work, releases locks under ordinary ownership/death rules and leaves surviving objects at their actual positions; no remote return, material duplication or refund of spent time/energy. No autonomous labor or unattended force application. No ongoing upkeep is charged merely for an annotation; placed material persists subject to existing physical processes, with no promised durability. Any maintenance is separately selected real inspection, adjustment or recovery at the disclosed operation cost. Compile these checks and state transitions into code, not repeated model adjudication.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":2,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"Study, registration, requests, queries, naming and mastery produce no experience benefit. This development adds no direct reward grant or protected-account write. A paid observation, informative failure or real familiar practice may be eligible only through an existing applicable experience handler, with source/revision/event deduplication and personal relevance. Re-inspecting an unchanged record is not new information. Any enabled benefit must have that handler's explicit bounded amount, cap, decay and cooldown; if no such bounded handler exists, award zero rather than inventing one. No pleasure or satisfaction is inferred from intended success, and no ongoing benefit arises from a dormant arrangement. Physical comfort is not established by this trial and cannot exceed the global cap of 10; nutrition is unchanged by mood. Do not alter reward accounts, budgets, goals or permissions.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Emit observable events only for actual paid examinations, manipulations, measured tests and recovery. Retain dated private evidence linked to actor, exact sources, revisions, method, units, uncertainty and process/arrangement IDs; do not disclose hidden source properties. Use reusable metadata with component, source references, actual geometry when known, state, progress, timestamp and evidence-event IDs. Assessment overlays are dashed non-solid annotations, clearly marked measured, estimated or unresolved; they are not material objects. Render a real placed vine or branch only after physical placement, with allocated material removed from the corresponding available source representation. Distinguish assessed, positioned, partially wrapped, wrapped-unverified, testing, slipped, damaged, paused, cancelled and recovered states. Never display a joined/success badge for registration, an incomplete wrap, unsupported force mechanics or an inconclusive test. Motion and force indicators must follow actual events, not merely the submitted target. Do not infer satisfaction from the visual result or make private findings public automatically.\\\"}]}\"}","logprobs":[]}

